    },
    {
      "chord_quality": "min7",
      "function_role": "active-giant-line-guide-chord-visualization",
      "narrative": "For Dm7 in active (changing-chord) contexts, Benson prescribes mapping single-note melodic fingerings directly onto guide chord shapes as the concrete fretboard method for internalizing Active Giant Lines. The student visualizes the guide chord shape under the fingers while executing the single-line melody. Chapter 13, p. 77.",
